# Line endings are normalised in the repository and checked out as LF everywhere.
# Why: the Makefile, shell scripts and container entrypoints run on Linux (WSL, Docker, CI).
# A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise write CRLF into the working tree,
# which breaks shebangs and can make shell recipes fail in ways that are hard to trace.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF so cmd.exe and PowerShell read them correctly.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never normalise or diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
